{"name":"Well Read","hex":"#7e633f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"well read","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of well-read."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/well_read"}],"entries":[{"title":"Intellectual","blocks":[{"text":"An intellectual is a person who engages in critical thinking, research, and reflection about the nature of reality, especially the nature of society and proposed solutions for its normative problems. Coming from the world of culture, either as a creator or as a mediator, the intellectual participates in politics, either to defend a concrete proposition or to denounce an injustice, usually by either rejecting, producing or extending an ideology, and by defending a system of values."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intellectual"},{"title":"Well","blocks":[{"text":"A well is an excavation or structure created on the earth by digging, driving, or drilling to access liquid resources, usually water. The oldest and most common kind of well is a water well, to access groundwater in underground aquifers. The well water is drawn up by a pump, or using containers, such as buckets that are raised mechanically or by hand. Water can also be injected back into the aquifer through the well. Wells were first constructed at least eight thousand years ago and historically vary in construction from a sediment of a dry watercourse to the qanats of Iran, and the stepwells and sakiehs of India. Placing a lining in the well shaft helps create stability, and linings of wood or wickerwork date back at least as far as the Iron Age."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Faryab-_village_dug_well.JPG/330px-Faryab-_village_dug_well.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Well"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg/500px-J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg/1280px-J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg/500px-J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The front page of L'Aurore (13 January 1898) featured Émile Zola's open letter J'Accuse…! asking the French President Félix Faure to resolve the Dreyfus affair.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJ%E2%80%99accuse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Edwards_Amasa_Park.jpg/500px-Edwards_Amasa_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Edwards_Amasa_Park.jpg/500px-Edwards_Amasa_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Congregational theologian Edwards Amasa Park proposed segregating the intellectuals from the public sphere of society in the United States.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdwards_Amasa_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg/1280px-Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The economist Milton Friedman identified the intelligentsia and the business class as interfering with capitalism.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APortrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Well-cistern.jpg/500px-Well-cistern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Well-cistern.jpg/1280px-Well-cistern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Well-cistern.jpg/500px-Well-cistern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The difference between a well and a cistern is in the source of the water: a cistern collects rainwater whereas a well draws from groundwater.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWell-cistern.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Tunis1960-150_hg.jpg/500px-Tunis1960-150_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Tunis1960-150_hg.jpg/1280px-Tunis1960-150_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Tunis1960-150_hg.jpg/500px-Tunis1960-150_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Camel drawing water from a well, Djerba island, Tunisia, 1960","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATunis1960-150_hg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/K%C3%BCckhoven_%28Erkelenz%29%2C_Brunnenbaureste_um_5300_v._Ch._.jpg/500px-K%C3%BCckhoven_%28Erkelenz%29%2C_Brunnenbaureste_um_5300_v._Ch._.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/K%C3%BCckhoven_%28Erkelenz%29%2C_Brunnenbaureste_um_5300_v._Ch._.jpg/1280px-K%C3%BCckhoven_%28Erkelenz%29%2C_